            heading: 'The Flower That Was a Trap',
            body: 'It began with a marriage arranged in secret. Hades, lord of the dead, had seen Persephone — Kore, "the Maiden," the only daughter of Demeter and Zeus — and desired her for his queen. He asked Zeus for her, and Zeus, who dared not refuse his brother and dared not tell Demeter, gave a consent that was also a concealment. Gaia herself prepared the trap: in the meadow of Nysa, where Kore wandered with the daughters of Ocean gathering roses and crocuses and violets, the earth sent up a flower no one had ever seen — a narcissus of unearthly beauty, a hundred blooms on a single stem, its sweetness reaching to heaven. The Maiden stretched out both hands to pluck it. The moment her fingers closed on the stem, the ground split open with a roar.',
